the way I think about it is that we've had these innovations—like remote hearings and digital filing—for years now, but they were never fully implemented because there was resistance from judges and court staff who didn’t want to change their routines. The pandemic forced everyone into a new normal where these tools became essential. It wasn’t that people suddenly realized it was possible; rather, they were pushed into doing it when traditional methods failed. That’s why I say the pandemic didn’t create the possibility—it revealed it.

